WEBVTT

1
00:00:11.308 --> 00:00:13.369
What do you mean Chuck and Dave are in prison?

2
00:00:13.389 --> 00:00:15.570
Brad: Just what I said.

3
00:00:16.130 --> 00:00:17.391
The mites have locked them up.

4
00:00:17.411 --> 00:00:21.552
Danny: Well, if we can't get them out, maybe we should leave.

5
00:00:21.572 --> 00:00:25.894
Brad: Do you want to stay small forever?

6
00:00:25.914 --> 00:00:27.035
Danny: No.

7
00:00:27.055 --> 00:00:29.336
Brad: We need Chuck and Dave.

8
00:00:29.748 --> 00:00:32.830
Brad: They are our only clue how to get us all back to normal.

9
00:00:32.850 --> 00:00:36.732
Danny: Well, I'm not going to stay small forever!

10
00:00:36.752 --> 00:00:40.375
Danny: Hold the straw steady—I'm coming up!

11
00:00:41.075 --> 00:00:47.659
Danny: Wow!

12
00:00:47.979 --> 00:00:48.780
You were right.

13
00:00:49.800 --> 00:00:51.401
There are a lot of mites!

14
00:00:52.202 --> 00:00:52.822
Brad: I know.

15
00:00:52.842 --> 00:00:55.324
Danny: So where are Chuck and Dave?

16
00:00:59.596 --> 00:01:00.856
Danny: What are we going to do?

17
00:01:00.876 --> 00:01:03.157
Brad: I don't know.

18
00:01:03.837 --> 00:01:05.778
We have got to get them out somehow.

19
00:01:06.738 --> 00:01:07.198
Danny: Okay.

20
00:01:07.498 --> 00:01:09.619
Mites. What are mites?

21
00:01:09.639 --> 00:01:14.360
Brad: Well, mites are small gross things.

22
00:01:14.380 --> 00:01:17.481
Danny: Besides that.

23
00:01:17.501 --> 00:01:20.082
Brad: They're invertebrates.

24
00:01:20.102 --> 00:01:22.202
Danny: Cool.

25
00:01:22.662 --> 00:01:23.483
What does that mean?

26
00:01:23.503 --> 00:01:25.783
Brad: They don't have spines.

27
00:01:26.663 --> 00:01:28.244
All insects are invertebrates.

28
00:01:29.804 --> 00:01:31.245
Danny: How does that help us?

29
00:01:31.265 --> 00:01:32.485
Brad: I don't know.

30
00:01:32.645 --> 00:01:33.786
You asked me what I know.

31
00:01:33.806 --> 00:01:39.428
Danny: Well, we know if we throw another rock, it will distract them.

32
00:01:39.448 --> 00:01:41.729
Brad: I'm fresh out of rocks.

33
00:01:43.650 --> 00:01:46.411
Danny: Hey, you've got your computer, don't you?

34
00:01:46.431 --> 00:01:48.692
Brad: I hadn't thought about it!

35
00:01:51.794 --> 00:01:52.534
It still works!

36
00:01:52.554 --> 00:01:54.415
Danny: Cool.

37
00:01:54.815 --> 00:01:56.896
You can throw it and distract them with that.

38
00:01:58.284 --> 00:01:59.925
Brad: I'm not going to break my computer!

39
00:01:59.945 --> 00:02:07.511
Brad: There's got to be something I can do with my computer Brad: I've got it!

40
00:02:07.531 --> 00:02:08.813
Danny: What?

41
00:02:09.873 --> 00:02:11.014
Brad: I can play a song!

42
00:02:11.615 --> 00:02:12.876
The mites will be curious.

43
00:02:12.896 --> 00:02:17.880
Brad: When they come to check it out, while they're here, [n3@we can go get the bullies.

44
00:02:17.900 --> 00:02:21.323
Danny: How will we get down from here?

45
00:02:21.343 --> 00:02:23.144
Brad: We'll have to jump.

46
00:02:23.825 --> 00:02:27.668
Danny: It's a long way down.

47
00:02:28.372 --> 00:02:29.533
We could hurt ourselves.

48
00:02:30.954 --> 00:02:38.880
Brad: Don't worry.

49
00:02:39.160 --> 00:02:40.481
I think we'll be all right.

50
00:02:45.004 --> 00:02:46.605
I sure hope you're right about this.

51
00:02:47.846 --> 00:02:52.689
Brad: Follow me.

52
00:02:52.990 --> 00:02:56.032
Run! Danny: Okay, now what?

53
00:02:59.820 --> 00:03:00.961
Brad: We're almost there.

54
00:03:03.182 --> 00:03:04.123
Grab this feather.

55
00:03:04.823 --> 00:03:06.244
We'll use it like a parachute.

56
00:03:06.264 --> 00:03:09.727
Brad: We're so tiny that we'll float softly to the ground.

57
00:03:09.747 --> 00:03:13.069
Danny: Okay, here we go.

58
00:03:13.089 --> 00:03:15.751
Brad: One, two, three!

59
00:03:15.771 --> 00:03:16.851
Danny: Now!
